# design explorations — standalone interactive HTML prototypes used to try a direction
# before it becomes app code. They are working material, not the product: they duplicate
# DS tokens by hand, bypass the token gates on purpose, and go stale the moment the real
# screen moves. Kept on disk so they stay openable; never pushed. The decisions they
# settle live in the brief under docs/design/proposals/, which *is* tracked.
docs/design/explorations/*
!docs/design/explorations/README.md

# bulk filing demo: server-side batch store
apps/dristi-app/.data/
